{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2VbzxMeH3Lzy3KWHPBKwQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, here's what I found about CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review forms:\n\n## Key Information Found\n\nThe search results show information about CoRL 2026's general structure and submission requirements, but a specific dedicated \"Reviewer Guidelines\" page for CoRL 2026 similar to what exists for previous years does not appear in the results. However, I can provide you with related information:\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Reference Material:**\nFor historical context, I found that CoRL builds its guidelines on those from ICML and NeurIPS, which provide extensive guidance to reviewers on how to write constructive reviews.\n\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL website directly or the OpenReview platform where submissions are managed (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference), as the specific reviewer guidelines page may not yet be fully indexed.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc4e0f6b-485a-459f-a513-fa7886e114ae","uuid":"bb4ec88d-f541-4a83-8dd4-d88c3df67fe0","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:56:36.247Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YYsSe82hbGKdJZXMX4se3B","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on my search results, here's what I found about CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review forms:\n\n## Key Information Found\n\nThe search results show information about CoRL 2026's general structure and submission requirements, but a specific dedicated \"Reviewer Guidelines\" page for CoRL 2026 similar to what exists for previous years does not appear in the results. However, I can provide you with related information:\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Reference Material:**\nFor historical context, I found that CoRL builds its guidelines on those from ICML and NeurIPS, which provide extensive guidance to reviewers on how to write constructive reviews.\n\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL website directly or the OpenReview platform where submissions are managed (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference), as the specific reviewer guidelines page may not yet be fully indexed."],"durationSeconds":6.2803661580000005}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtNGH4nUwPa8CDabgEmMQo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 review form reviewer guidelines scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"CommunityConnect 2025 Scoring Rubric for Abstracts 5 Excellent 4 Good 3 Fair 2\",\"url\":\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/9100a73e/files/uploaded/2025_Reviewer_Rating_Form_(Workshop_Rubric).pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond Paper-to-Paper: Structured Profiling and Rubric Scoring for Paper-Reviewer Matching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.05866\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, but the most specific results are from CoRL 2023 and 2024, not specifically CoRL 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Reviewer Guidelines\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete; be courteous and respectful. Start with the positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views in a discussion (e.g. agree to disagree).\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, either theoretical or empirical, and results are judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Limitations Evaluation\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation. However, obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nThe search results show guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but I did not find a specific scoring rubric document or detailed scoring scale for CoRL 2025. You may want to check the official CoRL 2025 website or OpenReview platform directly for the most current and detailed scoring rubric for this year's conference.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc4e0f6b-485a-459f-a513-fa7886e114ae","uuid":"8bcdb0d3-5572-45d5-ba47-c8c958e87821","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:56:39.624Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 review form reviewer guidelines scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015TZC8FPvMnJVntLQjYyPjZ","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/"},{"title":"CommunityConnect 2025 Scoring Rubric for Abstracts 5 Excellent 4 Good 3 Fair 2","url":"https://irp.cdn-website.com/9100a73e/files/uploaded/2025_Reviewer_Rating_Form_(Workshop_Rubric).pdf"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Beyond Paper-to-Paper: Structured Profiling and Rubric Scoring for Paper-Reviewer Matching","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.05866"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, but the most specific results are from CoRL 2023 and 2024, not specifically CoRL 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Reviewer Guidelines\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete; be courteous and respectful. Start with the positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views in a discussion (e.g. agree to disagree).\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, either theoretical or empirical, and results are judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Limitations Evaluation\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation. However, obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nThe search results show guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, but I did not find a specific scoring rubric document or detailed scoring scale for CoRL 2025. You may want to check the official CoRL 2025 website or OpenReview platform directly for the most current and detailed scoring rubric for this year's conference."],"durationSeconds":9.364233557}}
