{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QkB48TZZnFXMQFYt95jpRn","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form - Information Available\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot extract a complete review form with scoring dimensions and scales. The document provided contains **review criteria and desk reject guidelines only**, not the actual scoring rubric.\n\n## What IS Included:\n\n**Review Criteria:** Papers are evaluated on \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\" and \"their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\"\n\n**Desk Reject Criteria:** Papers may be rejected for formatting issues, anonymity violations, or scope concerns (lacking connection to physical robot learning).\n\n**Reviewer Qualifications:** Reviewers should demonstrate expertise through publications in robotics venues (CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, etc.) and machine learning conferences.\n\n## What IS NOT Included:\n\n- Numerical scoring scales (1-10, etc.)\n- Specific rubric descriptions for score levels\n- Acceptance thresholds or decision criteria\n- The actual review form structure\n\nTo obtain the complete review form with detailed scoring dimensions, you would need to access additional CoRL 2024 documentation or contact the organizing committee directly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc4e0f6b-485a-459f-a513-fa7886e114ae","uuid":"de0b1f7c-910c-4b16-b93b-eaa00f141137","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:56:50.651Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":133944,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form - Information Available\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot extract a complete review form with scoring dimensions and scales. The document provided contains **review criteria and desk reject guidelines only**, not the actual scoring rubric.\n\n## What IS Included:\n\n**Review Criteria:** Papers are evaluated on \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\" and \"their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\"\n\n**Desk Reject Criteria:** Papers may be rejected for formatting issues, anonymity violations, or scope concerns (lacking connection to physical robot learning).\n\n**Reviewer Qualifications:** Reviewers should demonstrate expertise through publications in robotics venues (CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, etc.) and machine learning conferences.\n\n## What IS NOT Included:\n\n- Numerical scoring scales (1-10, etc.)\n- Specific rubric descriptions for score levels\n- Acceptance thresholds or decision criteria\n- The actual review form structure\n\nTo obtain the complete review form with detailed scoring dimensions, you would need to access additional CoRL 2024 documentation or contact the organizing committee directly.","durationMs":3847,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BnGGTqKpbRY6QhHVWzZ6wJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided guidelines, the document **does not contain a complete review form with specific scoring dimensions, numerical scales, or detailed rubric descriptions for each score level**.\n\n## What Is Specified:\n\nThe guidelines outline **six evaluation dimensions** that reviewers must address:\n\n1. **Originality** - \"Are the problems or methods new?\" including novelty assessment and differentiation from prior work\n2. **Quality** - Technical soundness, claim support, methodological appropriateness, and honest evaluation of strengths/weaknesses\n3. **Clarity** - Writing quality, organization, and reproducibility of results\n4. **Significance** - Impact potential and state-of-the-art advancement\n5. **Relevance** - Robot learning applicability and CoRL audience interest\n6. **Limitations** - Assessment of author-reported limitations\n\n## Critical Gap:\n\nThe document provides **evaluation criteria descriptions but not scoring scales**. It specifies what reviewers should consider but does not detail:\n- Point scales (e.g., 1-5, 1-10)\n- Score level definitions\n- Numeric thresholds for acceptance/rejection\n- Specific rubric anchors for each rating\n\nThe guidelines emphasize **constructive evaluation** and reference external resources (ICML and NeurIPS) for additional guidance, suggesting the actual scoring mechanism may be housed in the OpenReview submission system rather than this introductory document."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc4e0f6b-485a-459f-a513-fa7886e114ae","uuid":"81b5081f-8b80-4210-aa5d-3477e32b8aea","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:56:53.223Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided guidelines, the document **does not contain a complete review form with specific scoring dimensions, numerical scales, or detailed rubric descriptions for each score level**.\n\n## What Is Specified:\n\nThe guidelines outline **six evaluation dimensions** that reviewers must address:\n\n1. **Originality** - \"Are the problems or methods new?\" including novelty assessment and differentiation from prior work\n2. **Quality** - Technical soundness, claim support, methodological appropriateness, and honest evaluation of strengths/weaknesses\n3. **Clarity** - Writing quality, organization, and reproducibility of results\n4. **Significance** - Impact potential and state-of-the-art advancement\n5. **Relevance** - Robot learning applicability and CoRL audience interest\n6. **Limitations** - Assessment of author-reported limitations\n\n## Critical Gap:\n\nThe document provides **evaluation criteria descriptions but not scoring scales**. It specifies what reviewers should consider but does not detail:\n- Point scales (e.g., 1-5, 1-10)\n- Score level definitions\n- Numeric thresholds for acceptance/rejection\n- Specific rubric anchors for each rating\n\nThe guidelines emphasize **constructive evaluation** and reference external resources (ICML and NeurIPS) for additional guidance, suggesting the actual scoring mechanism may be housed in the OpenReview submission system rather than this introductory document.","durationMs":5533,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
