{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015tXQ6UTVUsxDehF3gBeC6R","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Literature Gap Analysis — 2026-05-14\n2\t\n3\t## Overview\n4\t\n5\tReviewed 45 existing papers in literature_map.yaml against 6 coverage dimensions critical to the paper's narrative (\"Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\"). Identified 5 gaps, added 10 papers. Total: 55 papers.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Gap 1: Time Discretization Theory (CRITICAL)\n10\t\n11\t**Problem**: The paper argues variable-dt imagination fails in world-model RL, but the literature map lacked foundational theory on *why* time discretization matters for RL algorithms.\n12\t\n13\t**Added**:\n14\t| Paper | Venue | Role |\n15\t|-------|-------|------|\n16\t| Tallec et al. 2019 — \"Making Deep Q-learning Robust to Time Discretization\" | ICML | Theoretical foundation: Q-learning is inherently sensitive to δ; architecture + exploration must adapt. Directly supports our claim that RSSM cannot produce δ-invariant predictions. |\n17\t| Park et al. 2021 — \"SAR: Time Discretization-Invariant Safe Action Repetition\" | NeurIPS | Model-free solution achieving δ-invariance via adaptive state reaction during repetition. Contrast: model-free RL *can* be made robust to variable dt, but world-model RL cannot (our finding). |\n18\t| Wang & Beltrame 2024 — \"SEAC: Elastic Time Steps\" | arXiv | Variable-duration actions as part of action space. Model-free analog of our variable-dt imagination. |\n19\t\n20\t**Impact on narrative**: Strengthens C1 (degradation is expected) by grounding in δ-sensitivity theory. Provides clear distinction: model-free temporal abstraction has known solutions, world-model temporal abstraction does not.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Gap 2: Diagnostic Methodology Precedents (IMPORTANT)\n25\t\n26\t**Problem**: Our paper is a diagnostic/analysis paper, not a method paper. The literature map had no references to the \"what matters\" / factorial analysis tradition in RL.\n27\t\n28\t**Added**:\n29\t| Paper | Venue | Role |\n30\t|-------|-------|------|\n31\t| Engstrom et al. 2020 — \"Implementation Matters in Deep Policy Gradients\" | ICLR | Methodological precedent: code-level details (not algorithms) drive performance differences. Parallel to our finding that trained vs. untrained dt_embedding is the critical detail. |\n32\t| Andrychowicz et al. 2021 — \"What Matters for On-Policy Deep Actor-Critic Methods?\" | ICLR | Large-scale factorial study template (50+ choices, 250K agents). Direct methodological reference for our factorial design (dt_emb × subsample × horizon). |\n33\t\n34\t**Impact on narrative**: Legitimizes our diagnostic approach by citing established precedents. Useful for Introduction (\"following the tradition of systematic diagnostic studies in RL...\") and reviewer defense against \"no new algorithm\" critique (R5).\n35\t\n36\t---\n37\t\n38\t## Gap 3: Delusional Bias Follow-up (MODERATE)\n39\t\n40\t**Problem**: Had Lu et al. 2018 (formalizes delusional bias) but not ConQUR (2020), which proposes the first practical mitigation.\n41\t\n42\t**Added**:\n43\t| Paper | Venue | Role |\n44\t|-------|-------|------|\n45\t| Su et al. 2020 — \"ConQUR: Mitigating Delusional Bias in Deep Q-learning\" | ICML | Consistency-penalized Q-labels for delusional bias. Model-free mitigation; our delusional critic in MBRL is a different mechanism (temporal conditioning corruption, not policy-class constraint). |\n46\t\n47\t**Impact on narrative**: Completes the delusional bias literature arc: Lu 2018 (definition) → Su 2020 (mitigation in model-free) → our work (new instance in MBRL via dt_embedding).\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## Gap 4: MBRL Rollout Quality & Value Overestimation (CRITICAL)\n52\t\n53\t**Problem**: The paper's core finding is about imagination rollout quality, but the literature map lacked the most recent (ICLR 2025) work on rollout failures and value overestimation in MBRL.\n54\t\n55\t**Added**:\n56\t| Paper | Venue | Role |\n57\t|-------|-------|------|\n58\t| Frauenknecht et al. 2025 — \"On Rollouts in Model-Based RL\" | ICLR 2025 | Shows trajectory-sampling rollouts diverge after few steps and can *harm* policy learning. Proposes Infoprop (aleatoric/epistemic separation). Directly supports our findings; we identify a *specific* mechanism beyond general compounding error. |\n59\t| Voelcker et al. 2025 — \"MAD-TD: Model-Augmented Data stabilizes High UTD RL\" | ICLR 2025 | Value misgeneralization → instability at high UTD. Uses model data to fix values. Complementary mechanism: they fix replay distribution mismatch, we identify temporal conditioning corruption. |\n60\t\n61\t**Impact on narrative**: Critical for related work positioning. Our paper identifies a *specific, previously unknown* failure mechanism (dt_embedding-induced delusional critic) beyond the general rollout quality issues these papers address. Must cite to show awareness and differentiation.\n62\t\n63\t---\n64\t\n65\t## Gap 5: Latest Dreamer Evolution + Action Repeat (MODERATE)\n66\t\n67\t**Problem**: Literature map stopped at NE-Dreamer/DyMoDreamer for Dreamer extensions. Missing DreamerV4 and latest ICLR 2025 action repeat work.\n68\t\n69\t**Added**:\n70\t| Paper | Venue | Role |\n71\t|-------|-------|------|\n72\t| Hafner & Yan 2025 — \"DreamerV4: Training Agents Inside Scalable World Models\" | arXiv | Replaces RSSM with transformer; our RSSM-specific diagnosis still relevant as cautionary lesson for transformer world models. |\n73\t| Nie et al. 2025 — \"SDAR: Spatially Decoupled Action Repetition\" | ICLR 2025 | SOTA model-free action repeat. Advances variable-rate control in model-free; our work shows the obstacle in model-based. |\n74\t\n75\t**Impact on narrative**: DreamerV4 is essential for Discussion — our findings are RSSM-specific, but DreamerV4's transformer architecture may exhibit analogous issues if temporal conditioning is naive. SDAR extends the action repeat comparison.\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## Remaining Coverage Assessment\n80\t\n81\t| Dimension | Coverage | Notes |\n82\t|-----------|----------|-------|\n83\t| Value overestimation (model-free) | Excellent | Thrun 1993, Double DQN, TD3, SAC |\n84\t| Value overestimation (model-based) | Good → Excellent | Added MAD-TD, Frauenknecht |\n85\t| Delusional bias | Good → Excellent | Lu 2018 + ConQUR 2020 |\n86\t| Temporal abstraction (model-free) | Excellent | Options, FiGAR, TempoRL, SAR, SDAR, SEAC |\n87\t| Temporal abstraction (world models) | Excellent | THICK, Hieros, Director |\n88\t| Time discretization theory | Gap → Good | Added Tallec, Park, Wang |\n89\t| Diagnostic methodology | Gap → Good | Added Engstrom, Andrychowicz |\n90\t| MBRL rollout quality | Gap → Good | Added Frauenknecht, Barkley (existing) |\n91\t| Dreamer family | Excellent | V1-V4 + DreamerPro-era extensions |\n92\t| Reward prediction / objective mismatch | Excellent | DreamSmooth, HarmonyDream, Lambert 2020 |\n93\t| Seed variance / training instability | Excellent | Henderson, Nikishin, Qiao, Bjorck, Hussing |\n94\t| Evaluation methodology | Good | rliable (Agarwal 2021) |\n95\t\n96\t## No Major Remaining Gaps\n97\t\n98\tThe literature map now covers all dimensions needed for the related work section. Papers are tagged with appropriate `category` (background/evaluation/method-component/direct-competitor) and `role` descriptions for drafting.\n99\t\n100\t## Suggested Related Work Section Structure\n101\t\n102\t1. **Temporal abstraction in RL** — Options (Sutton 1999), FiGAR, TempoRL, SAR, SDAR → model-free success; THICK, Hieros, Director → world-model hierarchy approaches\n103\t2. **World-model RL** — Dreamer V1-V4, IRIS, TWM → architecture context\n104\t3. **Value overestimation and delusional bias** — Thrun 1993, Double DQN, TD3 → model-free; Lu 2018, ConQUR → delusional bias; MBPO, MOPO → model exploitation; MAD-TD, Frauenknecht → recent MBRL-specific\n105\t4. **Diagnostic methodology** — Engstrom 2020, Andrychowicz 2021, rliable → precedent for factorial analysis approach\n106\t5. **Time discretization** — Tallec 2019, Park 2021 → theoretical grounding for dt-sensitivity\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017z5tMZJZCNf1VL78rhSbS5","session_id":"bc4e0f6b-485a-459f-a513-fa7886e114ae","uuid":"a183b4b0-bb4c-4a5b-b10d-df467ce99bf5","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:59:15.304Z"}
